A NOTE ON WHAT THIS DOES AND DOESN'T DO
---------------------------------------

This is a plain-language summary, not legal advice, and it isn't part of the
licence terms above.

A browser game's source is fully readable by anyone who loads it. Opening the
page hands over the entire work: the levels, the solver, the artwork. This
notice gives you legal recourse against copying; it provides no technical
protection whatsoever, and there is no way to add any.

Minifying or obfuscating before publishing raises the effort required to reuse
the code, but a determined person still gets everything. Treat that as a speed
bump, not a lock.

If the commercial stakes here become meaningful, have a lawyer review this
before you rely on it. It was written to state your intent clearly, not to
survive a dispute.
